      "message": "vboot_hash_next_chunk() runs as a deferred routine from the HOOKS task, which is the lowest priority task. And, it tries to play nice by hashing small chunks at a time, to let other deferred routines run. It should only mess with your power signal output timing if:\n\n- Your power signals are changed from a deferred task or\n- You have some dependency on the shared mem buffer (eg. you call shared_mem_acquire() somewhere). vboot_hash_next_chunk() also uses this buffer, so you will have priority inversion if you depend on it.",
